<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  packaging/entitlements.plist - macOS hardened-runtime entitlements.

  WHY THESE TWO KEYS?
  PyInstaller-frozen apps embed CPython, which:
    1. allocates writable+executable memory pages for ctypes/cffi thunks
       (-> allow-unsigned-executable-memory), and
    2. loads .so libraries that were signed by US, not Apple
       (-> disable-library-validation).
  Without them a hardened-runtime app crashes at launch with a code-signing
  kill. These are the standard, Apple-documented exceptions for embedded
  interpreters - they do NOT disable notarization or the malware scan.

  ### WARN ###: for MAC APP STORE submission you must ALSO add the
  com.apple.security.app-sandbox entitlement and file-access entitlements
  (user-selected read-write for the Open/Save dialogs). Direct (DMG)
  distribution does not require the sandbox. See docs/packaging.md.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
